{"id": "unknown-2026-07-27-010", "date": "2026-07-27", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 31, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["oled_penetration"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "University of Toyama researchers developed the first crystalline OLED, offering promising performance", "content": "<p>Researchers from The University of Toyama have developed the world's first OLED that uses a non-epitaxial crystalline rubrene thin film as the emitter layer. To create this OLED device, the researchers combined an amorphous underlayer with precise annealing processes,&nbsp;</p><img data-entity-uuid=\"63a3ca04-a7fc-456e-864c-88308079229e\" data-entity-type=\"file\" src=\"https://www.oled-info.com/sites/default/files/inline-images/Toyoma-crystalline-emitter-OLED.png\" height=\"260\" alt=\"Toyoma Crystal", "sources": [{"name": "oled_info", "url": "https://www.oled-info.com/university-toyama-researchers-developed-first-crystalline-oled-offering", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "lg_elec-2026-07-27-011", "date": "2026-07-27", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 31, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": ["lg_elec", "lg_display", "samsung_elec"], "customers": ["lg_elec", "samsung_elec"], "suppliers": ["lg_display"]}, "topics": ["oled_penetration"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.9, "reasons": ["多公司提及", "供應鏈上下游同時提及"]}, "title": "Did LG and Samsung change strategy to exclusively target the high-end OLED market, and concede the lower-end to China?", "content": "<p>Something interesting is happening in Korea. Over the past few months, almost every significant move made by Samsung Display and LG Display has pointed in the same direction - upwards, towards the high end, and away from the volume tier of the OLED market.&nbsp;</p><div>\n  \n  <a href=\"https://www.oled-info.com/sites/default/files/2026-07/Korean-OLED-makers-2026-strategy-infographics.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">\n    \n    <img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://www.oled-info.com/sites/default/files/styles/la", "sources": [{"name": "oled_info", "url": "https://www.oled-info.com/lg-and-samsung-target-high-end-oled-market-do-they-concede-volume-oled-market", "type": "rss"}]}
